Here is an example of how you could create a fake chatbot using HTML and JavaScript:

HTML:
```
<!-- The Modal -->
<div id="myModal" class="modal">

  <!-- Modal content -->
  <div class="modal-content">
    randomTitle
    <span class="close">&times;</span>
    <p id="chatHistory"></p>
  </div>

</div>
```
JavaScript:
```
// array of messages
const messages = [
  {role: 'human', text: 'Hello, how are you?'},
  {role: 'bot', text: 'Hello! I am a fake chatbot. I am doing well, thank you.'},
  {role: 'human', text: 'That is good to hear. What can you do as a chatbot?'},
  {role: 'bot', text: 'I can simulate a conversation, but I don\'t have any real intelligence or the ability to perform tasks.'},
];

// function to display chat history
function displayChatHistory() {
  let chatHistory = '';
  messages.forEach(message => {
    chatHistory += `<strong>${message.role}:</strong> ${message.text}<br>`;
  });
  document.getElementById('chatHistory').innerHTML = chatHistory;
}

// open the modal and display chat history
document.getElementById('myModal').style.display = 'block';
displayChatHistory();

// add event listener for close button
document.getElementsByClassName('close')[0].addEventListener('click', function() {
  document.getElementById('myModal').style.display = 'none';
});

// add event listener for window click to close modal
window.addEventListener('click', function(event) {
  if (event.target == document.getElementById('myModal')) {
    document.getElementById('myModal').style.display = 'none';
  }
});
```
This example uses a modal, which is a child window that requires users to interact with it before they can return to the parent window. The chat history is stored in an array of messages and is displayed using the `displayChatHistory()` function. The `displayChatHistory()` function is called when the modal is opened. The modal is closed when the user clicks on the close button or anywhere outside of the modal.

You can customize this example to fit your specific needs. This is just a basic example, you can use css to style the modal and add more functionality with javascript.

