Here's a simple C++ function that converts markdown-formatted text to HTML. This function only handles a small subset of markdown features, specifically bold and italic text. It can be extended to handle other markdown features as needed.

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <regex>

std::string markdownToHtml(std::string& markdownText) {
    // Replace **bold** text with <strong>bold</strong>
    std::regex boldPattern(R"(\*\*(.*?)\*\*)");
    markdownText = std::regex_replace(markdownText, boldPattern, "<strong>$1</strong>");

    // Replace *italic* text with <em>italic</em>
    std::regex italicPattern(R"(\*(.*?)\*)");
    markdownText = std::regex_replace(markdownText, italicPattern, "<em>$1</em>");

    return markdownText;
}
```

